<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's health workers hold second stoppage.</title>
<headline>Morocco's health workers hold second stoppage.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thousands of Moroccan health workers in the public sector started their second two-day strike in a week on Wednesday to press for pay increases and compensation for medical risks, their union said.</p>
<p>Last week, they held a two-day stoppage and decided to renew it this week in protest against what they described as the &quot;government's indifference to our claims.&quot;</p>
<p>The Democratic Labour Confederation said in a statement sent to Reuters on Wednesday that 92 to 100 percent of staff observed the protest in the country's main medical centres.</p>
<p>The union said there were 3,500 doctors and 40,000 paramedical staff in the public sector. It was not clear if all were members of the union.</p>
<p>Health ministry officials were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
